<div class="alert alert-warning">
  <strong>Usage Disclaimer:</strong> AI-generated content may be incorrect,
  biased, incomplete, or misleading. Always review, verify, and edit AI
  output before use. Before uploading data to any AI tool, please review the
  <a href="https://it.tufts.edu/sites/default/files/uploaded-files/2018-09/information-classification-handling_2018-06-18_0.pdf"
  target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tufts Information Classification and Handling Policy</a>
  and the <a href="https://access.tufts.edu/data-finder" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Data Storage Finder</a>.
  Do not enter any restricted data into the tool without formal TTS review.
  For requirements and best practices, please refer to Tufts&rsquo;
  <a href="https://it.tufts.edu/ai/guidance-using-ai-tufts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Guidelines for Use of Generative AI Tools</a>.
</div>
<h5>How to use this application</h5>
<p class="mb-2">
  These values let you connect to an open-weights large language model (LLM)
  from any software that uses an
  <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-openapi" target="_blank"
  rel="noopener">OpenAI-compliant API</a>, including the OpenAI Python,
  LangChain, curl, or Visual Studio extensions such as
  <a href="https://continue.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Continue.dev</a>
  (see below).
</p>
<h5>Direct Connection information</h5>
<div class="d-grid gap-3">
  <div class="input-group">
    <span class="input-group-text" style="width: 6em;"><strong>
      Base URL
    </strong></span>
    <span id="base-url" class="form-control"><code id="base-url">
      http://<%= host %>.pax.tufts.edu:<%= port %>
    </code></span>
    <button class="btn btn-light far fa-copy copy-btn" type="button"
      data-target="base-url" style="aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;"
      title="Copy Base URL"></button>
  </div>
  <small class="form-text text-muted mt-n2">
    The server address to configure in your client (usually as the
    <code>base_url</code>/<code>apiBase</code> setting, often with
    <code>/v1</code> appended).
  </small>
  <div class="input-group">
    <span class="input-group-text" style="width: 6em;"><strong>
      Model ID
    </strong></span>
    <% if use_router == "0" %>
    <span id="model-id" class="form-control"><code id="model-id">
      <%= File.basename(model_file) %>
    </code></span>
    <button class="btn btn-light far fa-copy copy-btn" type="button"
      data-target="model-id" style="aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;"
      title="Copy Model ID"></button>
    <% else %>
    <span class="form-control text-muted">
      Router mode: multiple models available, see <code>/v1/models</code>
    </span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <small class="form-text text-muted mt-n2">
    The <code>model</code> name to send with each request. Some clients
    require this even if the server only hosts one model.
  </small>
  <div class="input-group">
        <span class="input-group-text" style="width: 6em;"><strong>
      API Key
    </strong></span>
    <span id="api-key" class="form-control"><code id="api-key">
      <%= password %></code>
    </span>
    <button class="btn btn-light far fa-copy copy-btn" type="button"
      data-target="api-key" style="aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;"
      title="Copy API Key"></button>
  </div>
  <small class="form-text text-muted mt-n2">
    Sent as an <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> token (or
    <code>apiKey</code>/<code>api_key</code> setting) to authenticate your
    requests. Anyone with this key can use the server, so keep it private.
  </small>
</div>
<hr />
<div>
  <h5>VS Code Connection Information</h5>
  <p class="mb-1">
    Copy this text and paste it in your <code>config.yaml</code> to use this
    model in VS Code with <a href="https://continue.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Continue.dev</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="input-group">
    <pre id="continue-config" class="form-control" style="white-space: pre-wrap; margin-bottom: 0;">  - name: Tufts LLM Endpoint
    provider: openai
    model: <%= use_router == "0" ? File.basename(model_file) : "AUTODETECT" %>
    apiBase: http://<%= host %>.pax.tufts.edu:<%= port %>/v1
    apiKey: <%= password %>
    roles:
      - chat
      - edit
      - apply</pre>
    <button class="btn btn-light far fa-copy copy-btn" type="button"
      data-target="continue-config" style="aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;"
      title="Copy Continue config"></button>
  </div>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="d-flex gap-2">
  <a href="/rnode/<%= host %>/<%= port %>/"
    class="btn btn-primary" id="launch-button">
    <i class="fa fa-eye"></i> Launch Web UI
  </a>
  <a href="/pun/sys/dashboard/files/fs/<%= output_log %>"
    class="btn btn-secondary">
    <i class="fa fa-file-text"></i> View Server Log
  </a>
</div>

<script>
  document.getElementById('launch-button')
    .addEventListener('mouseover', function() {
      localStorage.setItem(
        'LlamaCppWebui.config', '{"apiKey":"<%= password %>"}'
      );
    });
  document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      const targetId = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
      const code = document.getElementById(targetId).innerText;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(code);
      btn.classList.remove('fa-copy');
      btn.classList.add('fa-check-square');
      setTimeout(() => {
        btn.classList.remove('fa-check-square');
        btn.classList.add('fa-copy');
      }, 1500);
    });
  });
</script>
